    "breadcrumb": "Swing Catalyst Támogatás \u003e Szoftver és Funkciók",
    "content": "A Swing Catalyst Mozgásrögzítési Eszköz Felhasználóinak Fontos Felhívásai\nKöszönjük, hogy a mi mozgáskövetési megoldásunkat választotta golfütésének elemzéséhez. Annak érdekében, hogy a legjobb tapasztalatot szerezhesse és teljes mértékben megértse eszközünk lehetőségeit és korlátait, kérjük, olvassa el gondosan az alábbi fontos felhívásokat:\nPontosság és Megbízhatóság\nKorlátozott Mennyiségi Tesztelés: A mi mozgáskövetési rendszere minimális mennyiségi tesztelésen esett át. Ezért az elemzés pontossága és megbízhatósága néhány alkalmazás esetén nem feltétlenül felel meg a szakmai standardoknak.\nElőre Betanított Modellek: Az eszköz előre betanított modelleket (RTMPose és RTMDet) használ, amelyeket nem optimalizáltak kifejezetten a golfütés-elemzésre. Ennek következtében a mozgáskövetés eredményei pontatlanságokat vagy következetlenségeket tartalmazhatnak, különösen a modelleket betanító adatok által nem támogatott kameranézetek esetén. Az előre betanított modellekkel kapcsolatos további információkért lásd az alábbi referenciákat:\nRTMDet (Person detection): 2212.07784\nRTMPose (Persons’s body keypoints): 2303.07399, mmpose/projects/rtmpose at main · open-mmlab/mmpose · GitHub Limitations of Pre-Trained Models\nGeneral-Purpose Training: The underlying models were trained on general datasets and may not capture the specific nuances and biomechanics of golf swings.\nPose Estimation Errors: Rapid movements and complex poses common in golf swings may under some circumstances lead to errors in pose estimation and motion tracking (see Environmental and Technical Constraints below).\nPC specifications (minimum):\nSee Swing Catalyst Motion Capture FAQ\nEnvironmental and Technical Constraints\nCamera Quality: The effectiveness of the motion tracking is highly dependent on the quality of the video input. Low-resolution, shaky, or blurry videos can significantly reduce accuracy.\nLighting Conditions: Poor or uneven lighting can adversely affect the detection and tracking of motion and poses of the golf swing.\nCamera Angles: The tool is optimized for frontal face-on and sagittal down-the-line camera views. Deviations from these angles may result in less accurate analysis. It is not recommended to use the top-down or back view of the golfer due to a high number of occluded body key points.\nOccluded body points: Occluded body points are detected with less precision compared to visible body points. The user should interpret the position of occluded body points with caution.\nDown-the-line view and DLP projector for launch monitors: Occasionally, DLP projector can affect performance of the motion capture models in down-the-line view. Sufficient lighting conditions is very important for these setups to prevent errors in the motion capture models.\n2D inference only: The Swing Catalyst Motion Capture Tool does only provide 2D inference in the selected camera view. Inter-session deviation of the camera setup may affect the comparison of results. Identical camera setup should be used when comparing golf swing trials.\nUser Responsibility\nProfessional Advice: This tool is intended for informational and recreational purposes only and should not replace professional coaching, instruction, or biomechanical analysis.\nVerification of Results: Users should independently verify the accuracy of the analysis before making any changes to their swing or training regimen based on the tool’s output.\nPrivacy and Data Security\nData Processing: Videos and data processed by the tool may be stored for analysis purposes by your explicit consent\nData Storage and Deletion: We do not store your videos or personal data beyond the duration necessary for analysis unless explicitly agreed upon.\nThird-Party Access: We do not share your data with third parties without your explicit consent.\nUser Consent: By using the tool, you consent to the processing of your data as outlined in our privacy policy.\nNo Liability\nUse at Your Own Risk: The use of this tool is at your own risk. We are not liable for any inaccuracies in the analysis or any decisions made based on the tool’s output.\nLimitation of Warranty: The tool is provided “as is” without any warranties, express or implied, including but not limited to accuracy, reliability, or fitness for a particular purpose.\nUpdates and Improvements\nOngoing Development: Our motion tracking tool is under continuous development. Features, functionalities, and performance may change over time without prior notice.\nNo Guaranteed Updates: While we strive to improve the tool, we do not guarantee regular updates or enhancements.\nIntellectual Property\nThird-Party Models and Licenses: The tool incorporates RTMPose and RTMDet models, which are subject to their respective open-source licenses. Users must comply with these licenses when using the tool.\nUser Content Rights: You retain ownership of your video content. By using the tool, you grant us permission to process your content solely for the purpose of providing the analysis service.\nAppropriate Use\nPersonal Use and Commercial Use:\nCompliance with Laws: Users are responsible for ensuring that their use of the tool complies with all applicable local, state, national, and international laws and regulations.\nTechnical Support and Contact Information\nAssistance: If you encounter any issues or have questions about using the tool, please contact our support team.\nContact Details: [Insert Contact Information Here]\nBy proceeding to use our motion tracking tool for golf swing analysis, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to these disclosures.\nLast updated: 2025-03-05 | View on official support site",
    "description": "Swing Catalyst mozgásrögzítés felhasználóinak fontos biztonsági és pontossági nyilatkozatai",
